Not in my (hacked up) version of NetHack.  In my game:

+ Spellpoints are regenerated about 4 times more slowly.
+ Spellpoints are only gained every other level.
+ It costs much more to cast a spell.

+ It is far easier to memorize a spell.
+ Spells are memorized forever. (Unless Maud visits...)
  And can be cast without fear of forgetting them.
+ Wizards and priests get perks.
+ Identify and Extra Healing have been upgraded to avoid abuse...
  (It is prohibitively expensive to cast these often...)

It makes for a very different game.  (Characters with low INT and WIS like
Valkyrie and Barbarian can forget about high level spells altogether.) 
Wizards and priests have different fighting styles!  Now, I often wish for a
spellbook of magic mapping before I would wish for a ring of conflict or 
amulet of lifesaving.  Magic mapping makes Hell much more manageable.  
(Well, only every 3rd level, or so.  It takes a *very* long time to 
recuperate from high-level spells.)

If you have a mac, I'd be happy to give you my version.  It's too cumbersome
to mail people source files...

